            <ArticleTitle>B(C6F5)3 catalysed reduction of para-quinone methides and fuchsones to access unsymmetrical diaryl- and triarylmethanes: elaboration to beclobrate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8393-8401</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02007d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mild and efficient method for the synthesis of unsymmetrical diaryl- and triarylmethanes through a B(C6F5)3 catalyzed reduction of para-quinone methides and fuchsones respectively, using the Hantzsch ester as a reducing source has been developed. Detailed mechanistic investigations revealed that the reaction actually proceeds through a Lewis acid-base pair complex derived from B(C6F5)3 and the Hantzsch ester.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
